  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square pastel painting of a hillside of lobed trees, rocks and hidden faces descending to a lake, with a sun setting behind clouds.",
    "description": "A square oil painting in pastel colour with thin dark outlines. A pale blue sky with long outlined clouds and a yellow setting sun sits over a strip of blue water. Below it, bands of cream and yellow fields, then a slope of lobed trees and rounded rocks in peach, mint, lilac and green. In the lower right, large rounded forms carry eyes and mouths, like sleeping faces in the hillside. A lilac disc like a flying saucer or a mushroom cap tilts at upper left, and a cluster of pine like spikes rises at centre. The surface is matte with soft, flat colour.",
    "impression": "A gentle hillside at sunset that turns out to be full of faces when you look at it long enough. It is quieter than the other Desertland pieces and more like a real landscape, with the hidden creatures as a secret for a patient viewer. The title suggests it was made for someone.",
